*> Implementation test of proto/src/chunk24.cob: PB-PUT-CHUNK-24 and PB-GET-CHUNK-24, the body of the
*> Level Chunk With Light packet for a dimension of any number of sections (docs/protocol/06-chunk-
*> format.md §2 to §7): heightmaps, the section buffer with 16-bit paletted containers, block entities
*> and the light of sections + 2 indices (26 for the 24 sections of the overworld).
*> The worked example is the 24-section fixture of contract/fixtures/wire; the facts asserted about it
*> were read from the fixture with an independent decoder. A second, small chunk has its bytes
*> computed independently of the codec.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CHUNK24.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY PROTO.
 COPY PROTO REPLACING LEADING ==PB-== BY ==PK-==.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 64.
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-HEX                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-HEX-2               PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-PTR                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-S                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-OFFSET              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BYTE                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EQUAL               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SAME                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SUM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LABEL               PIC X(120).
 01 WS-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SECTIONS            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HM-BITS             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HM-MASK             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BLOCK-GBITS         BINARY-LONG VALUE 16.
 01 WS-BIOME-GBITS         BINARY-LONG VALUE 7.
 01 WS-BE-COUNT            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-BE-MAX              BINARY-LONG VALUE 16.
 01 WS-BE-DATA-MAX         BINARY-LONG VALUE 1024.
 01 WD-X                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WD-Z                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WD-HM-MASK             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WD-BE-COUNT            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HM-VALUES.
    05 WS-HM               BINARY-LONG OCCURS 1536 TIMES.
 01 WD-HM-VALUES.
    05 WD-HM               BINARY-LONG OCCURS 1536 TIMES.
 01 WS-COUNTS.
    05 WS-COUNT-ENTRY      BINARY-LONG OCCURS 48 TIMES.
 01 WD-COUNTS.
    05 WD-COUNT-ENTRY      BINARY-LONG OCCURS 48 TIMES.
 01 WS-STATES.
    05 WS-STATE            BINARY-LONG OCCURS 98304 TIMES.
 01 WD-STATES.
    05 WD-STATE            BINARY-LONG OCCURS 98304 TIMES.
 01 WS-BIOMES.
    05 WS-BIOME            BINARY-LONG OCCURS 1536 TIMES.
 01 WD-BIOMES.
    05 WD-BIOME            BINARY-LONG OCCURS 1536 TIMES.
 01 WS-BE-HEADS.
    05 WS-BE-HEAD          BINARY-LONG OCCURS 80 TIMES.
 01 WD-BE-HEADS.
    05 WD-BE-HEAD          BINARY-LONG OCCURS 80 TIMES.
 01 WS-BE-DATA             PIC X(1024).
 01 WD-BE-DATA             PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-SKY-STATES.
    05 WS-SKY-STATE        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WD-SKY-STATES.
    05 WD-SKY-STATE        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WS-BLK-STATES.
    05 WS-BLK-STATE        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WD-BLK-STATES.
    05 WD-BLK-STATE        BINARY-LONG OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WS-SKY-ARRAYS.
    05 WS-SKY-ARRAY        PIC X(2048) OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WD-SKY-ARRAYS.
    05 WD-SKY-ARRAY        PIC X(2048) OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WS-BLK-ARRAYS.
    05 WS-BLK-ARRAY        PIC X(2048) OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WD-BLK-ARRAYS.
    05 WD-BLK-ARRAY        PIC X(2048) OCCURS 26 TIMES.
 01 WS-CHAR                PIC X.
 01 WS-ARRAY               PIC X(2048).
 01 WS-SEEN.
    05 WS-SEEN-FLAG        PIC 9 OCCURS 36000 TIMES.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PB-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     CALL "PB-INIT" USING PK-BUFFER WS-CAPACITY
     PERFORM FIXTURE-CASES
     PERFORM SMALL-CASES
     PERFORM MINIMAL-CASES
     PERFORM PUT-ERROR-CASES
     PERFORM GET-ERROR-CASES
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-FREE" USING PK-BUFFER
     STOP RUN.

*> ---- the 24-section worked example: read it, assert what it holds, write it back ----
 FIXTURE-CASES.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-PATH
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/wire/play-s2c-2e-level-chunk-with-light-standard-24-sections.hex"
         TO WS-PATH
     CALL "TEST-LOAD-HEX" USING WS-PATH PB-BUFFER
     CALL "PB-GET-UBYTE" USING PB-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     MOVE 24 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE 9 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE 16 TO WS-BLOCK-GBITS
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BIOME-GBITS
     PERFORM DECODE-CALL
     MOVE "fixture: decodes with no error and reads every byte" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM OBSERVE-STATUS
     MOVE "0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: chunk x z and the heightmap types 1, 4, 5 (mask 50)" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WD-X TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-Z TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-HM-MASK TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "0 0 50" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: every column of the three heightmaps is 128, the others stay 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 1536
         IF WD-HM(WS-I) = 128
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         ELSE
             ADD WD-HM(WS-I) TO WS-SUM
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-SUM TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "768 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: non-empty counts 4096 for sections 0 to 17, 0 above, fluid counts 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT WS-SUM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > 24
         IF WD-COUNT-ENTRY(WS-S * 2 - 1) = 4096
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         END-IF
         ADD WD-COUNT-ENTRY(WS-S * 2) TO WS-SUM
         IF WS-S > 18 AND WD-COUNT-ENTRY(WS-S * 2 - 1) NOT = 0
             ADD 1000 TO WS-SUM
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-SUM TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "18 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     PERFORM FIXTURE-STATE-CASES
     PERFORM FIXTURE-LIGHT-CASES
     MOVE "fixture: writing the decoded chunk again gives the fixture bytes" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM COPY-DECODED-TO-INPUT
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PK-BUFFER
     MOVE 46 TO WS-BYTE
     CALL "PB-PUT-UBYTE" USING PK-BUFFER WS-BYTE
     PERFORM ENCODE-CALL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OFFSET
     CALL "TEST-SLICE-EQUALS" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET PK-BUFFER WS-EQUAL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PK-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-EQUAL TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     COMPUTE WS-N = PB-LENGTH - PK-LENGTH
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "0 1 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED.

 FIXTURE-STATE-CASES.
*>   Section 0: the bedrock layer (state 88, cells 1 to 256) then stone (state 1).
     MOVE "fixture: section 0 holds bedrock 88 in its first 256 cells and stone 1 after" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 4096
         IF WS-I <= 256 AND WD-STATE(WS-I) NOT = 88
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         END-IF
         IF WS-I > 256 AND WD-STATE(WS-I) NOT = 1
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM OBSERVE-NUMBER
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
*>   Sections of one value: stone in 1 to 3 and 9 to 17, air in 18 to 23 (0-based).
     MOVE "fixture: single-value sections are stone 1 (1 to 3, 9 to 17) or air 0 (18 to 23)" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > 23
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 4096
             COMPUTE WS-J = WS-S * 4096 + WS-I
             EVALUATE TRUE
                 WHEN WS-S >= 1 AND WS-S <= 3 AND WD-STATE(WS-J) NOT = 1
                     ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
                 WHEN WS-S >= 9 AND WS-S <= 17 AND WD-STATE(WS-J) NOT = 1
                     ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
                 WHEN WS-S >= 18 AND WD-STATE(WS-J) NOT = 0
                     ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
             END-EVALUATE
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM OBSERVE-NUMBER
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
*>   Distinct states of sections 4 to 8 (the indirect 4, 5, 6 and 8 bit sections and the direct one).
     MOVE "fixture: distinct states of sections 4 to 8 are 2, 20, 40, 200 and 4096" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 4 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > 8
         PERFORM COUNT-DISTINCT-STATES
         PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "2 20 40 200 4096" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: section 5 uses ids 100 to 119, section 8 entry i is i * 7 mod 35723" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 4096
         COMPUTE WS-J = 5 * 4096 + WS-I
         IF WD-STATE(WS-J) < 100 OR WD-STATE(WS-J) > 119
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         END-IF
         COMPUTE WS-J = 8 * 4096 + WS-I
         IF WD-STATE(WS-J) NOT = FUNCTION MOD((WS-I - 1) * 7, 35723)
             ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM OBSERVE-NUMBER
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
*>   Biomes: distinct values of sections 0 to 8.
     MOVE "fixture: distinct biomes of sections 0 to 8 are 1 2 2 2 4 8 64 1 1" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     PERFORM VARYING WS-S FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-S > 8
         INITIALIZE WS-SEEN
         MOVE 0 TO WS-N
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 64
             COMPUTE WS-J = WS-S * 64 + WS-I
             IF WS-SEEN-FLAG(WD-BIOME(WS-J) + 1) = 0
                 MOVE 1 TO WS-SEEN-FLAG(WD-BIOME(WS-J) + 1)
                 ADD 1 TO WS-N
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
         PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "1 2 2 2 4 8 64 1 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED.

*> WS-S is the 0-based section; leaves the number of distinct states in WS-N.
 COUNT-DISTINCT-STATES.
     INITIALIZE WS-SEEN
     MOVE 0 TO WS-N
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 4096
         COMPUTE WS-J = WS-S * 4096 + WS-I
         IF WS-SEEN-FLAG(WD-STATE(WS-J) + 1) = 0
             MOVE 1 TO WS-SEEN-FLAG(WD-STATE(WS-J) + 1)
             ADD 1 TO WS-N
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM.

 FIXTURE-LIGHT-CASES.
     MOVE "fixture: sky light states of the 26 indices (arrays at 0 and 20, empty 1 and 2)"
         TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 26
         MOVE WD-SKY-STATE(WS-I) TO WS-N
         PERFORM ADD-DIGIT
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "211" & "00000000000000000" & "2" & "00000" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: block light states (array at 4, every other index empty)" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 26
         MOVE WD-BLK-STATE(WS-I) TO WS-N
         PERFORM ADD-DIGIT
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "11112" & "111111111111111111111" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "fixture: the sky arrays are 0xff (15), the block array 0x11" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(256) TO WS-CHAR
     MOVE ALL "z" TO WS-ARRAY
     INSPECT WS-ARRAY REPLACING ALL "z" BY WS-CHAR
     IF WD-SKY-ARRAY(1) NOT = WS-ARRAY OR WD-SKY-ARRAY(21) NOT = WS-ARRAY
         ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
     END-IF
     IF WD-BLK-ARRAY(5) NOT = ALL X"11"
         ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
     END-IF
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM OBSERVE-NUMBER
     MOVE "0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED.

*> ---- a two-section chunk (min_y 0, height 32: heightmaps of 6 bits) with bytes worked out apart ----
 SMALL-CASES.
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE "small: written chunk has the independently computed bytes before the light arrays"
         TO WS-LABEL
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM ENCODE-CALL-PB
     MOVE "fffffffd0000000501041a06d85523cc2460c0061548f30918301e05523cc2460c079b048f30918301e6d803cc2460c079b6"
         TO WS-HEX(1:100)
     MOVE "15030918301e6d855202460c079b61548f018301e6d85523cc00c079b61548f309001e6d85523cc246079b61548f30918306"
         TO WS-HEX(101:100)
     MOVE "d85523cc2460c0061548f30918301e05523cc2460c079b048f30918301e6d803cc2460c079b615030918301e6d855202460c"
         TO WS-HEX(201:100)
     MOVE "079b61548f018301e6d85523cc00c079b61548f309001e6d85523cc246079b61548f30918306d85523cc2460c0061548f309"
         TO WS-HEX(301:100)
     MOVE "18301e05523cc2460c079b000000018301e6d810000000000000000010000005000100020237fffb050a010001610700f001"
         TO WS-HEX(401:100)
     MOVE "2cc801000101010801020104" TO WS-HEX(501:24)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE 262 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-HEX TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-SLICE-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT TL-OBSERVED
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "small: light arrays follow as count, length 2048 and the bytes (0x0f sky, 0xbb block)"
         TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 262 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE 8 TO WS-COUNT
     MOVE "018010" & "0f0f0f0f0f" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-SLICE-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ", sky" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 2313 TO WS-OFFSET
     MOVE "018010" & "bbbbbbbbbb" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-SLICE-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER WS-OFFSET WS-COUNT TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) ", block" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "small: error and total length" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "0 4364" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
*>   Read it back: every input field returns.
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     PERFORM DECODE-CALL
     MOVE "small: decodes with no error and reads every byte" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM OBSERVE-STATUS
     MOVE "0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "small: x, z, heightmap mask, block entity count" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WD-X TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-Z TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-HM-MASK TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-BE-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "-3 5 16 2" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "small: heightmap, counts, states, biomes, block entities and light equal the input"
         TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SAME
     IF WD-HM-VALUES = WS-HM-VALUES AND WD-COUNTS(1:16) = WS-COUNTS(1:16)
             AND WD-STATES(1:32768) = WS-STATES(1:32768)
             AND WD-BIOMES(1:512) = WS-BIOMES(1:512)
             AND WD-BE-HEADS(1:40) = WS-BE-HEADS(1:40) AND WD-BE-DATA(1:7) = WS-BE-DATA(1:7)
             AND WD-SKY-STATES(1:16) = WS-SKY-STATES(1:16)
             AND WD-BLK-STATES(1:16) = WS-BLK-STATES(1:16)
             AND WD-SKY-ARRAY(1) = WS-SKY-ARRAY(1) AND WD-BLK-ARRAY(4) = WS-BLK-ARRAY(4)
         MOVE 1 TO WS-SAME
     END-IF
     MOVE WS-SAME TO WS-N
     PERFORM OBSERVE-NUMBER
     MOVE "1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED
     MOVE "small: heightmap columns come back at their own index" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE WD-HM(4 * 256 + 2) TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-HM(4 * 256 + 11) TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-HM(4 * 256 + 256) TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "3 30 6" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED.

*> The reference input: 2 sections, heightmap type 4 only (values column * 3 mod 33), section 0 air,
*> section 1 stone 1 with fluid count 5, biomes 0 and 2, two block entities and 4 light indices.
 SET-SMALL.
     INITIALIZE WS-HM-VALUES WS-COUNTS WS-STATES WS-BIOMES WS-BE-HEADS WS-BE-DATA
         WS-SKY-STATES WS-BLK-STATES WS-SKY-ARRAYS WS-BLK-ARRAYS
     MOVE -3 TO WS-X
     MOVE 5 TO WS-Z
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE 6 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE 16 TO WS-HM-MASK
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 255
         COMPUTE WS-HM(4 * 256 + WS-I + 1) = FUNCTION MOD(WS-I * 3, 33)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 4096 TO WS-COUNT-ENTRY(3)
     MOVE 5 TO WS-COUNT-ENTRY(4)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 4097 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 8192
         MOVE 1 TO WS-STATE(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 65 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > 128
         MOVE 2 TO WS-BIOME(WS-I)
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BE-COUNT
     MOVE 3 TO WS-BE-HEAD(1)
     MOVE -5 TO WS-BE-HEAD(2)
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BE-HEAD(3)
     MOVE 5 TO WS-BE-HEAD(4)
     MOVE 7 TO WS-BE-HEAD(5)
     MOVE 15 TO WS-BE-HEAD(6)
     MOVE 300 TO WS-BE-HEAD(7)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BE-HEAD(8)
     MOVE 200 TO WS-BE-HEAD(9)
     MOVE 0 TO WS-BE-HEAD(10)
     MOVE X"0a010001610700" TO WS-BE-DATA(1:7)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SKY-STATE(1)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SKY-STATE(2)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-BLK-STATE(3)
     MOVE 2 TO WS-BLK-STATE(4)
     MOVE ALL X"0f" TO WS-SKY-ARRAY(1)
     MOVE ALL "z" TO WS-BLK-ARRAY(4)
     MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(188) TO WS-CHAR
     INSPECT WS-BLK-ARRAY(4) REPLACING ALL "z" BY WS-CHAR.

*> ---- the smallest chunk: one air section, no heightmaps, no block entities, no light ----
 MINIMAL-CASES.
     PERFORM SET-MINIMAL
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM ENCODE-CALL-PB
     MOVE "minimal: written chunk is 25 bytes of the hand-assembled form" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "0000000100000002" & "00" & "08" & "0000000000000000" & "00000000000000" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-HEX TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-BUFFER-HEX" USING PB-BUFFER TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS
     PERFORM DECODE-CALL
     MOVE "minimal: reads back with no error, no heightmaps and no block entities" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     COMPUTE WS-N = PB-LENGTH - PB-POS
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-X TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-Z TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-HM-MASK TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE WD-BE-COUNT TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "0 0 1 2 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM ASSERT-OBSERVED.

 SET-MINIMAL.
     INITIALIZE WS-HM-VALUES WS-COUNTS WS-STATES WS-BIOMES WS-BE-HEADS WS-BE-DATA
         WS-SKY-STATES WS-BLK-STATES
     MOVE 1 TO WS-X
     MOVE 2 TO WS-Z
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE 6 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HM-MASK WS-BE-COUNT.

*> ---- writer rejections: PB-ERROR and nothing appended ----
 PUT-ERROR-CASES.
     MOVE "no sections" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "65 sections" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 65 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "heightmap bits 0" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HM-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "heightmap bits 32" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 32 TO WS-HM-BITS
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "heightmap mask with bit 6" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 80 TO WS-HM-MASK
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "heightmap value 64 does not fit 6 bits" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 64 TO WS-HM(4 * 256 + 3)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "heightmap negative value" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-HM(4 * 256 + 3)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "non-empty count 4097" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 4097 TO WS-COUNT-ENTRY(3)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "negative non-empty count" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-COUNT-ENTRY(1)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "fluid count 4097" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 4097 TO WS-COUNT-ENTRY(4)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "negative block state in section 1" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-STATE(5000)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "negative biome in section 1" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-BIOME(100)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "negative block entity count" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-BE-COUNT
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity local x 16" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 16 TO WS-BE-HEAD(1)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity local z -1" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-BE-HEAD(8)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity y 32768" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE 32768 TO WS-BE-HEAD(7)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity y -32769" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -32769 TO WS-BE-HEAD(2)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity negative type" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-BE-HEAD(9)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity negative data length" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE -1 TO WS-BE-HEAD(5)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity data that is not a network compound" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE X"0801000161" TO WS-BE-DATA(1:5)
     MOVE 5 TO WS-BE-HEAD(5)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity compound followed by a stray byte" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE X"0a00" TO WS-BE-DATA(1:2)
     MOVE FUNCTION CHAR(256) TO WS-BE-DATA(3:1)
     MOVE 3 TO WS-BE-HEAD(5)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED
     MOVE "block entity compound cut short" TO WS-LABEL
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     MOVE X"0a0100" TO WS-BE-DATA(1:3)
     MOVE 3 TO WS-BE-HEAD(5)
     PERFORM PUT-REJECTED.

 PUT-REJECTED.
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM ENCODE-CALL-PB
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 put rejects " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-LENGTH TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "1 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> ---- reader rejections: PB-ERROR and PB-POS back at the start ----
 GET-ERROR-CASES.
     PERFORM SET-SMALL
     CALL "PB-RESET" USING PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM ENCODE-CALL-PB
     MOVE "get: 3 sections asked of a 2-section buffer" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 3 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: 1 section asked leaves bytes in the section buffer" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE "get: heightmap bits 5 expect 22 Longs, not 26" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 5 TO WS-HM-BITS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 6 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE "get: no sections asked" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE "get: 65 sections asked" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 65 TO WS-SECTIONS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE "get: heightmap bits 0" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 0 TO WS-HM-BITS
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 6 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE "get: one block entity of capacity 1 for 2" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 1 TO WS-BE-MAX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 16 TO WS-BE-MAX
     MOVE "get: block entity data capacity 3 for 7 bytes" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE 3 TO WS-BE-DATA-MAX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 1024 TO WS-BE-DATA-MAX
     MOVE "get: the buffer cut 100 bytes short" TO WS-LABEL
     SUBTRACT 100 FROM PB-LENGTH
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SECTIONS
     MOVE 6 TO WS-HM-BITS
     MOVE "get: heightmap type 6" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 01 06 00" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: 7 heightmaps" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 07" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: the same heightmap type twice" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 02 04 1a" TO WS-HEX
     MOVE ALL "0" TO WS-HEX(27:416)
     MOVE " 04 1a" TO WS-HEX(443:6)
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: 5 heightmap Longs where 26 are due" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 01 04 05" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: section buffer of 2097153 bytes" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 81808001" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: section buffer longer than the packet" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 40" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: section buffer 9 bytes for a section of 8" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 09 0000000000000000 00 0000000000000000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: negative non-empty count" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 ffff0000 00000000 00 00000000000000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: fluid count 4097" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 00001001 00000000 00 00000000000000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: block entity count -1" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 ffffffff0f" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: block entity of a String root" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 01 37fffb05 08 0000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: block entity compound cut short" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 01 37fffb05 0a 01" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: block entity with a negative type" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 01 37fffb ffffffff0f" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: block entity packed byte but no Y" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 01 37" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: light mask bit 7 for 3 light indices" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000000000000000 00 0180 00 00 00 00 00" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX
     MOVE "get: invalid palette in the block states" TO WS-LABEL
     MOVE "00000001 00000002 00 08 0000 0000 04ffffffff0f 0000" TO WS-HEX
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED-HEX.

*> Fills the buffer from WS-HEX (spaces ignored) and reads it as a one-section chunk.
 GET-REJECTED-HEX.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-HEX-2
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-HEX) "." DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-HEX-2
     CALL "TEST-FILL-HEX" USING WS-HEX-2 PB-BUFFER
     PERFORM GET-REJECTED.

 GET-REJECTED.
     MOVE 0 TO PB-POS PB-ERROR
     PERFORM DECODE-CALL
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE PB-POS TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     MOVE "1 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

*> ---- calls and helpers ----
 ENCODE-CALL.
     CALL "PB-PUT-CHUNK-24" USING PK-BUFFER WS-X WS-Z WS-SECTIONS WS-HM-BITS WS-HM-MASK
         WS-HM-VALUES WS-COUNTS WS-STATES WS-BIOMES WS-BLOCK-GBITS WS-BIOME-GBITS WS-BE-COUNT
         WS-BE-HEADS WS-BE-DATA WS-SKY-STATES WS-SKY-ARRAYS WS-BLK-STATES WS-BLK-ARRAYS.

 ENCODE-CALL-PB.
     CALL "PB-PUT-CHUNK-24" USING PB-BUFFER WS-X WS-Z WS-SECTIONS WS-HM-BITS WS-HM-MASK
         WS-HM-VALUES WS-COUNTS WS-STATES WS-BIOMES WS-BLOCK-GBITS WS-BIOME-GBITS WS-BE-COUNT
         WS-BE-HEADS WS-BE-DATA WS-SKY-STATES WS-SKY-ARRAYS WS-BLK-STATES WS-BLK-ARRAYS.

 DECODE-CALL.
     CALL "PB-GET-CHUNK-24" USING PB-BUFFER WD-X WD-Z WS-SECTIONS WS-HM-BITS WD-HM-MASK
         WD-HM-VALUES WD-COUNTS WD-STATES WD-BIOMES WS-BLOCK-GBITS WS-BIOME-GBITS WS-BE-MAX
         WS-BE-DATA-MAX WD-BE-COUNT WD-BE-HEADS WD-BE-DATA WD-SKY-STATES WD-SKY-ARRAYS
         WD-BLK-STATES WD-BLK-ARRAYS.

 COPY-DECODED-TO-INPUT.
     MOVE WD-X TO WS-X
     MOVE WD-Z TO WS-Z
     MOVE WD-HM-MASK TO WS-HM-MASK
     MOVE WD-HM-VALUES TO WS-HM-VALUES
     MOVE WD-COUNTS TO WS-COUNTS
     MOVE WD-STATES TO WS-STATES
     MOVE WD-BIOMES TO WS-BIOMES
     MOVE WD-BE-COUNT TO WS-BE-COUNT
     MOVE WD-BE-HEADS TO WS-BE-HEADS
     MOVE WD-BE-DATA TO WS-BE-DATA
     MOVE WD-SKY-STATES TO WS-SKY-STATES
     MOVE WD-BLK-STATES TO WS-BLK-STATES
     MOVE WD-SKY-ARRAYS TO WS-SKY-ARRAYS
     MOVE WD-BLK-ARRAYS TO WS-BLK-ARRAYS.

*> Observes PB-ERROR and the unread byte count.
 OBSERVE-STATUS.
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     MOVE PB-ERROR TO WS-N
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER
     COMPUTE WS-N = PB-LENGTH - PB-POS
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER.

 OBSERVE-NUMBER.
     PERFORM START-OBSERVED
     PERFORM ADD-NUMBER.

 ASSERT-OBSERVED.
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "test chunk24 " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-LABEL) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 START-OBSERVED.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     MOVE 1 TO WS-PTR.

 ADD-NUMBER.
     MOVE WS-N TO WS-EDIT
     IF WS-PTR > 1
         STRING " " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR
     END-IF
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.

 ADD-DIGIT.
     MOVE WS-N TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-PTR.
 END PROGRAM TEST-CHUNK24.
 COPY PROTOTEST.
